\details{
Removes every WildObs addition from a data package so it matches a published Camtrap DP
version exactly, and can be read by standard consumers such as the \pkg{camtrapdp} R
package, GBIF (via \code{camtrapdp::write_dwc()}) and Agouti. Returns the converted package
with a report of every change.

The conversion works in this order:
\enumerate{
\item \strong{Descriptor}: every key the target profile does not define is removed, at
any depth, e.g. \code{WildObsMetadata}, \code{versionControlWildObs}, \code{project$DPID},
\code{contributors[]$ROR}, and the per-deploymentGroup blocks and \code{timeZone} in
\code{temporal}. Empty (\code{NA}) values are dropped too, since Camtrap DP treats a missing
property as absent rather than null. \code{profile} and \code{version} are pointed at the
target version. \code{spatial} is left untouched: it is GeoJSON, which allows extra
members.
\item \strong{Tables}: \code{deployments}, \code{media} and \code{observations} keep only the target
schema's fields, in the target order, and their inline schemas are replaced with the
TDWG table-schema URL. The values in every kept column are unchanged. The
\code{covariates} table is removed unless \code{keep_covariates = TRUE} (Camtrap DP allows
extra tables, so keeping it still validates).
}
Four value changes are made, because the values would otherwise fail validation or
break \pkg{camtrapdp} functions:
\itemize{
\item \code{taxonomic[]$vernacularNamesEnglish} becomes \code{vernacularNames$eng}, the
Camtrap DP form, so common names are kept.
\item A \code{taxonRank} outside the Camtrap DP list (e.g. \code{subclass}) is rounded up to the
nearest broader rank in it (e.g. \code{class}), so a record never claims more precision
than its identification had.
\item A \code{relatedIdentifierType} of \code{RAiD}, which DataCite does not list, becomes
\code{Handle}.
\item Media rows whose \code{filePath} or \code{fileMediatype} break the Camtrap DP pattern
(e.g. a path on a contributor's own computer) are removed, and any observation whose
\code{mediaID} pointed at one has its \code{mediaID} set to \code{NA}. This can empty the media
table, in which case a warning says so.
}

The input must hold all three Camtrap DP tables in memory, as packages from
\code{wildobs_dp_download(..., media = TRUE)} do; a package without one stops with an
explanation. The original \code{dp} is never modified. The result keeps its tables in
\code{resources} only (read them with \code{frictionless::read_resource()}), without the extra
\code{dp$data} copy, so \code{frictionless::write_package()} writes a clean Camtrap DP package.
